# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files for more about ignoring files.
#
# Temporary files generated by your text editor or operating system
# belong in git's global ignore instead:
# `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/git/ignore` or `~/.config/git/ignore`

# Ignore bundler config.
/.bundle

# Ignore all environment files.
/.env*

# `cafe dev` GENERATES this from cafaye.yml and rewrites it on every run — the
# file says so in its own first line ("Do not edit: every run rewrites this
# file"). It is build output shaped like a source file, which is why it needs
# saying here rather than relying on it being untracked by accident: an
# untracked generated file is one `git add -A` away from being committed, and
# from there it is a merge conflict nobody can resolve by reading it.
#
# The tracked `docker-compose.yml` is the opposite case and is NOT ignored. That
# one is hand-written, it is the service's declaration of its own tenant, and it
# is reviewed.
/cafe.dev.compose.yaml

# Ignore all logfiles and tempfiles.
/log/*
/tmp/*
!/log/.keep
!/tmp/.keep

# Ignore pidfiles, but keep the directory.
/tmp/pids/*
!/tmp/pids/
!/tmp/pids/.keep

# Ignore storage (uploaded files in development and any SQLite databases).
/storage/*
!/storage/.keep
/tmp/storage/*
!/tmp/storage/
!/tmp/storage/.keep

# Ignore key files for decrypting credentials and more.
/config/*.key

# Git worktrees created inside the checkout (the fleet's worker layout).
# Their files are another branch's working copies, not this tree's: untracked
# here, invisible to `git add -A`, and never committed by accident.
wt/
keyring/
secrets/
